The reviewed source covers `sign-envelope-field.ts` (L1–284), `execute-tsp-sign.ts` (L8–167), and `signing-status-envelope.ts` (L1–81).

**Source-grounded review**

**Envelope must be PENDING for field signing**
When `signEnvelopeFieldRoute` reaches the status check — after the `deletedAt` guard at L99 — `envelope.status !== DocumentStatus.PENDING` throws `AppErrorCode.INVALID_REQUEST`.

```105:109:packages/trpc/server/envelope-router/sign-envelope-field.ts
    if (envelope.status !== DocumentStatus.PENDING) {
      throw new AppError(AppErrorCode.INVALID_REQUEST, {
        message: `Document ${envelope.id} must be pending for signing`,
      });
    }
```

**CSC path treats already-SIGNED recipient as idempotent; no envelope-status guard is visible in the reviewed window**
When `executeTspSign` reaches the idempotency check — after session, token, and session-ownership checks at L88–L108 — `recipient.signingStatus === SigningStatus.SIGNED` returns `{ outcome: 'already_signed' }` with no `envelope.status` check anywhere in the reviewed window (L8–L167).

```113:115:packages/ee/server-only/signing/csc/execute-tsp-sign.ts
  if (recipient.signingStatus === SigningStatus.SIGNED) {
    return { outcome: 'already_signed' };
  }
```

**Recipient already-signed guard fires only after the PENDING check passes**
When `signEnvelopeFieldRoute` reaches L111 — only after the PENDING guard at L105 has not thrown — `recipient.signingStatus === SigningStatus.SIGNED || field.recipient.signingStatus === SigningStatus.SIGNED` throws `AppErrorCode.INVALID_REQUEST`.

```111:115:packages/trpc/server/envelope-router/sign-envelope-field.ts
    if (recipient.signingStatus === SigningStatus.SIGNED || field.recipient.signingStatus === SigningStatus.SIGNED) {
      throw new AppError(AppErrorCode.INVALID_REQUEST, {
        message: `Recipient ${recipient.id} has already signed`,
      });
    }
```

**Open questions**

1. Does `executeTspSign` apply an `envelope.status === PENDING` guard in the body beyond L167, the end of the reviewed window? A test calling `cscSignEnvelopeRoute` with a COMPLETED envelope and a non-SIGNED recipient would confirm whether the CSC path enforces envelope PENDING independently of the recipient idempotency check.

2. When recipient-level state satisfies the `isComplete` condition at L65–L69 of `signing-status-envelope.ts` but the envelope row has not yet transitioned to `DocumentStatus.COMPLETED`, can the route's `'PROCESSING'` status persist indefinitely if the post-signing completion handler fails? Document or test what mechanism is expected to advance the envelope row and whether any timeout or retry policy bounds the `PROCESSING` window.

3. In `signEnvelopeFieldRoute`, the ASSISTANT field query at L42–L51 filters on the target recipient's `signingStatus` and `signingOrder` but not on `envelope.status`, so the field lookup can resolve for a non-PENDING envelope before the PENDING guard fires at L105; does intended policy require ASSISTANT callers against a non-PENDING envelope to receive `INVALID_REQUEST` rather than `NOT_FOUND`? A test against a COMPLETED envelope would pin the intended guard ordering before any refactor.

